From: Alex Brodsky <122503996+Albro3459@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:58:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 69/73] File links skip output from sessions on other machines

Warp's web build counts every session as remote, so it handed the host page paths from SSH and container sessions too. The host checked them on its own machine and underlined files that happened to exist there, like /etc/hosts or ~/.zshrc, and Cmd+click opened the wrong machine's file. A block now gets no file links when its host differs from the pane's first shell, found by following each session's spawning session up from the prompt. A block keeps the host it recorded, so restored blocks are covered too. An unknown host keeps the old behaviour, and plain ssh without Warpify still links, since its output belongs to the local shell. Desktop is unchanged

Verified with a link detection test and wasm checks with and without terminal_only
---
 app/src/terminal/model/session.rs             |  4 ++
 app/src/terminal/view/link_detection.rs       | 59 ++++++++++++++++---
 app/src/terminal/view/link_detection_tests.rs | 40 +++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 95 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

